@startuml activity-ai-analysis
!include style.iuml
title Requesting an AI analysis (activity, UC-05)

|Clinician or pathologist|
start
:Open the patient's "AI analyses" and tap Request;
|Backend|
if (Patient has an active AI_ANALYSIS consent?) then (no)
  :Refuse: CONSENT_REQUIRED;
  stop
endif
if (At least one screening record?) then (no)
  :Refuse: CLINICAL_RECORD_REQUIRED;
  stop
endif
if (An analysis already queued or running?) then (yes)
  :Refuse: AI_JOB_IN_PROGRESS;
  stop
endif
:Collect the inputs: a keyed pseudonym (no name or NRC),
clinical values, de-identified copies of the scans;
note right: files without a de-identified\ncopy are listed, never sent
:Create the job (QUEUED), audit it,
and answer 202 at once;
:Queue worker: job RUNNING;
|AI service|
:Model router runs each module whose input exists:
imaging (U-Net, ResNet-50), clinical ANN, slides,
then the fusion step;
note right
  Today every module is a labelled MOCK:
  its numbers come from a hash of the job id,
  never from the patient's values or images.
end note
:Explanations for each module, or the reason
there is none (never invented);
|Backend|
if (Valid answer within the time limit?) then (yes)
  :Store the report in MongoDB (ai_reports, with
  provenance MOCK and the disclaimer);
  :Job SUCCEEDED;
else (no)
  :Job FAILED or TIMED_OUT, with the reason;
endif
|Clinician or pathologist|
:The app polls the job and shows the report:
"DEVELOPMENT MOCK DATA — NOT A CLINICAL RESULT"
first, then probability range, grade group,
modules used or skipped, explanations;
stop
@enduml
